--TEST--
Inside its own constructor, a `readonly` property is written only through `$this` (`rule:classes/readonly-is-written-once`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The other node finished its own constructor already, so writing its `readonly`
// property here is a second write to it. The write through `$this` is allowed.
class Node {
    public readonly uint $id;

    public function constructor(uint $id, ?Node $previous) {
        $this->id = $id;
        if ($previous != null) {
            $previous->id = $id - 1;
        }
    }
}

var $a = new Node(1, null);
// covers: lang:classes/properties
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0782]: `Node::$id` is `readonly`, so only `Node`'s constructor writes it
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
